nodecode-super-artifacts is a rewrite of Super-Artifacts's Super-Artifacts/plugins:

  https://github.com/Super-Artifacts/plugins
  commit dce02981a179a09dad6509fe58a3a7b8cf020735
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Super Artifacts (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the one hosted MCP server the original's mcp.json named, spoken
directly. The transport is here -- an initialize handshake with its
notifications/initialized notice, an Mcp-Session-Id when the server names one,
and either answer the streamable HTTP transport chooses, a JSON body or a
server-sent event -- and five tools register on it: super_whoami,
super_publish, super_data, super_artifacts, and super_tool, which reaches
every other tool the server offers (super_upload, super_templates,
super_comments, super_data_query, super_share, super_artifact_set,
super_help and the rest) by its own name. super_publish forwards a slug, a
title, the whole HTML and a visibility that is private unless the call says
otherwise, and answers the URL the page went live at. The original's skill is
the cell's manual topic, (help :super-artifacts), kept in its voice: call
super_whoami first and name the account, publish private, never widen who can
open an artifact unless the person asked, one stable slug per subject so every
update is a version, report the rows that are there and never invent one.

The sign-in is ported as /super-artifacts signin: OAuth 2.1 device
authorization against the product's own discovery document -- register this
client, ask for a device code, print the page and the code, poll the token
endpoint in the background, keep the token at 0600 in the cell's state folder,
and refresh it when it ages out.

Left out, and why: Hermes's own plugin and MCP plumbing -- `hermes plugins
install', `hermes mcp add --auth oauth', `hermes mcp login --flow device',
/reload-mcp and the plugins dashboard -- is the cell's section, its /super-artifacts
command and its own token file, since a Nodecode cell has no Hermes CLI to
call. The portable plugin.yaml/plugin.json manifest and the after-install.md
page are the .asd and the README. The browser authorization-code flow is left
out: the device flow is the one that works over SSH and in a terminal, and it
mints the same token. The MCP server's own tool schemas are not copied: the
tools here carry the arguments the skill used, and any further tool is reached
through super_tool, so a tool the server adds later still works without a
release of this cell.
